{"result":"{
  "id": "261750785",
  "title": "Development Standards",
  "type": "page",
  "created": "",
  "updated": "",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/261750785",
  "space": {
    "key": "SFCC",
    "name": "Adobe SFCC"
  },
  "version": 2,
  "attachments": [],
  "content": {
    "value": "<p>General day-to-day coding conventions for the Zimmermann PWA Kit. For the pattern used to override a base Salesforce component vs. build a new Zimmermann-specific one, see <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/261881857\">Component Override Strategy</a>.</p><h2>Naming conventions</h2><table><thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Convention</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New Zimmermann files and folders</td><td><code>camelCase</code></td><td><code>backInStockButton/</code>, <code>useWishlist.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Overrides of Salesforce base files</td><td>Keep upstream kebab-case exactly</td><td><code>product-tile/index.tsx</code></td></tr><tr><td>Component named export</td><td>Matches folder name</td><td><code>BackInStockButton</code> exported from <code>backInStockButton/</code></td></tr><tr><td>Component props type</td><td>Component name + <code>Props</code></td><td><code>BackInStockButtonProps</code></td></tr><tr><td>Hook files</td><td><code>.ts</code> (not <code>.tsx</code>)</td><td><code>useWishlist.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Hook export</td><td>Matches filename</td><td><code>useWishlist</code></td></tr><tr><td>Callback props</td><td><code>onEventName</code></td><td><code>onAddToCart</code>, <code>onClose</code></td></tr><tr><td>Identifiers and copy</td><td>Australian spelling</td><td><code>colour</code>, <code>centre</code>, <code>organisation</code></td></tr><tr><td>Override files</td><td>Keep upstream Salesforce spelling verbatim</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table><p>TypeScript only inside <code>overrides/</code>. No <code>.js</code> or <code>.jsx</code> files. Run <code>npx tsc --noEmit</code> before finishing any task that touches <code>overrides/</code>.</p><p>No <code>any</code> without an inline comment explaining why a narrower type is impossible.</p><p>Prefer <code>type</code> over <code>interface</code> for component props and shared shapes.</p><h2>Design tokens</h2><p>Design tokens (colours, typography, spacing) live in <code>overrides/app/theme/foundation/</code> — <strong>frozen (Tier 1)</strong>, owned by the UI Designer. Do not modify except to sync with Figma; ask the UI Designer if a needed colour/font isn't in the token set.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"037d973a-5490-4b95-8189-04a9948d50af\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">tsx</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[// ✅ correct — uses the token\n<Text color=\"brand.primary\" fontSize=\"md\">…</Text>\n\n// ❌ wrong — hardcoded value\n<Text color=\"#1a1a1a\" fontSize=\"16px\">…</Text>]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>Per-component theme overrides (button variant, link styles, etc.) live in <code>overrides/app/theme/components/</code> — Tier 2 (protected), owned by the UI Designer.</p><h2>Common shared components</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Path</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Header</td><td><code>overrides/app/components/header/</code></td><td>Tier 2 — coordinate with both squads before touching</td></tr><tr><td>Page container</td><td><code>overrides/app/components/pageContainer/</code></td><td>Wraps page-level layout</td></tr><tr><td>App config</td><td><code>overrides/app/components/_app-config/</code></td><td>Tier 2</td></tr><tr><td>Button</td><td><code>overrides/app/components/button/</code></td><td>Zimmermann button override</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For icons, use <code>@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/components/icons</code>. If a required icon is missing, get it from Figma or ask the UI Designer — do not substitute a visually different one.</p><h2>Styling</h2><ol><li>Chakra UI props first.</li><li><code>.scss</code> file alongside the component only when Chakra props cannot achieve the required result.</li></ol><p>Never hardcode hex colours, pixel spacing values, or raw font sizes in component props.</p><h2>Storybook</h2><p>Every component exported from <code>overrides/app/components/</code> or <code>overrides/app/pages/</code> must have a <code>.stories.tsx</code> file.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>What goes here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Foundation/</code></td><td>Design token visualisations</td></tr><tr><td><code>Elements/</code></td><td>Generic building blocks (Button, Input, Badge)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Commerce/</code></td><td>Commerce-specific components (ProductTile, OrderSummary)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Layout/</code></td><td>Global shell (Header, Footer, DrawerMenu)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Forms/</code></td><td>Form assemblies (AddressForm, CheckoutContactForm)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Pages/</code></td><td>Full page assemblies (PDP, PLP, Cart)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Every story file needs a <code>Default</code> named export. Add named exports for meaningful states (<code>Loading</code>, <code>OutOfStock</code>) — not for every prop combination.</p><h2>Testing</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Tool</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Unit</td><td>Vitest</td><td>Data mapping, transforms, hook logic in isolation</td></tr><tr><td>Component interaction</td><td>Storybook <code>play</code></td><td>User interactions (clicks, form fills, focus)</td></tr><tr><td>E2E</td><td>Playwright</td><td>Full user journeys across pages</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Vitest tests co-locate with source as <code>*.test.ts</code>.</p><h2>Before opening a PR</h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"87dd3c00-3784-4bff-a0f3-013af43154a9\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">bash</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[npx tsc --noEmit    # TypeScript must be clean\nnpm run lint        # lint must pass\nnpm run test        # unit tests must pass]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>Claude Code's <code>/code-quality</code> skill runs a pre-PR audit of changed files; <code>/pr-checklist</code> generates a structured PR description.</p><h2>File protection tiers</h2><p>Not all files are equally safe to edit.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>What</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Tier 1 — Frozen</strong></td><td>Design tokens, shared commerce hooks, SSR/config, CI/CD</td><td>Stop. Get owner approval before any change.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Tier 2 — Protected</strong></td><td>Global shell, shared product components, translations, shared hooks</td><td>PR requires a second reviewer. Notify the owner.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Unclassified</strong></td><td>A squad's own feature components and pages</td><td>Normal feature-branch workflow.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Full lists live in the repo's <code>.claude/rules/frozenFiles.md</code> and <code>.claude/rules/protectedFiles.md</code>.</p>",
    "format": "storage"
  },
  "emoji": "1f680"
}"}

