    ],
    "content": {
      "value": "This page defines our sprint cadence so everyone understands the rhythm of planning, execution, review, and continuous improvement. Use it as a shared reference for key ceremonies, expected timelines, team responsibilities, and decision points throughout each sprint cycle.\n\nThis page consists of:\n\n* <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/322207767/Meeting+Cadences#Governance-Forum-Framework>\n* <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/322207767/Meeting+Cadences#Sprint-Cadences>\n* <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/322207767/Meeting+Cadences#Governance-Forums>\n\nGovernance Forum Framework\n--------------------------\n\nThe connective tissue between delivery and leadership. A set of structured forums for senior stakeholders to stay informed, make key decisions, and ensure the programme stays aligned to business objectives and on track for delivery.\n\n![image-20260713-133654.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/322207767/child/attachment/att319881283/download)\n\nSprint Cadences\n---------------\n\nOur sprint cadences are the engine of how we work — a structured rhythm of ceremonies that keep the team connected, aligned and continuously delivering\n\n| **Cadence** | **When** | **Suggested Audience** | **Purpose** | **Output** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Sprint Planning | Tuesday (First day of Sprint) | Core Squads | Align on the sprint goal, confirm capacity, and select the work the team will commit to delivering | Sprint goal, committed backlog items, initial sprint plan |\n| Daily Stand Up | Every Day | Core Squads | Inspect progress, surface blockers, and coordinate the team's work for the next 24 hours. | Updated plan, identified blockers, follow-up actions |\n| Backlog Refinement | Every Thursday | Core Squads | Review upcoming backlog items, clarify requirements, split stories, and estimate effort. | Refined and prioritized backlog items ready for future planning |\n| Dependency & Risk Review | Every Thursday | Program Management | Review cross-team dependencies, identify delivery risks, agree on mitigations, and confirm ownership of follow-up actions. | Updated dependency and risk log, mitigation actions, assigned owners |\n| Sprint Showcase | Monday (Final Day of Sprint) | Core Squads, Program Mgmt, Stakeholders | Demonstrate completed work, gather feedback, and discuss changes to priorities or scope. | Feedback, accepted work, updated product backlog |\n| Sprint Retrospective | Monday (Final Day of Sprint) | Core Squads | Reflect on how the team worked together and identify improvements for the next sprint. | Improvement actions for the next sprint |\n| User Story Reviews | Weekly | Business Analysts, Emma, Lucy, Rebecca | To interrogate, refine, and collectively sign off on stories before they hit the sprint | Approved User Stories in JIRA |\n| Design Alignment | Weekly | Designers, Business Analysts, Rebecca, Emma | A critical checkpoint to ensure designs have been approved - this will help keep design and delivery moving as one | Endorsed designs that will feed into user stories1 |\n\nGovernance Forums\n-----------------\n\n| **Cadence** | **When** | **Suggested Audience** | **Purpose** | **Output** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Project Status Update | Fortnightly | Rebecca, Emma, Lucy, Simon, Tim, Peter, Tash, Izzy, Alrick, Marjo | The single source of truth for programme health. These updates give stakeholders a clear and honest view of where we are, where we're headed, and what needs attention | Traffic light system of delivery status, along with key asks |\n| Partners Forum | Weekly | Business Analysts, SFCC Architect, FED Lead, Partners as needed | Placeholder for third party partners to help support key clarifications and questions that the core squads might have | Key documentation and decisions |\n| Key Outstanding Actions | Weekly (up to Sprint 3) | Izzy, Tash, Rebecca, Emma, Lucy | Help support the progress and unblocking of key areas that the squads need to progress their delivery | Status update on key outstanding actions |",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

